                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Gardenarium is digital art.\n\nIt has a beginning and an end, and it has the mechanics of a first person platformer, but it isn't a game. There is no challenge. If you are looking for one and run through the game, you can \"beat it\" in 10 minutes, but that's like saying it took you 20 minutes to beat the museum.\n\nI spent 30 minutes. I felt a bit overwhelmed and disoriented at times. I'm curious how this looks in 3D or VR. But I definitely like the feel of it, the accerated growing, as if I was some god of fertility, the way it changes color as I pick up cans, the characters. I haven't seen anything like it before.\n\nIs it worth 4,99? I got the game in a bundle, so I didn't have to decide. For its size, you'd probably wish the price of admission was less.\n\n[i]This game runs fine on my old Windows XP computer.[/i]",
